<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Backup and device-transfer rules for API 31+ (audit F-22).

  `allowBackup="true"` was set with nothing declared, which leaves the decision
  to platform defaults. These state it outright:

  - cloud-backup and device-transfer both carry the trip, because losing a
    collection on a phone upgrade would be unrecoverable — there is no account
    to restore from (con-0004-no-backend-no-accounts).

  Both blocks previously carried an <exclude> for
  "CapacitorStorage.temp_quiz_session.xml", meaning to hold back the in-flight
  quiz sidecar. No such file has ever existed and the line matched nothing
  (pm-0002). `temp_quiz_session` is a *key* inside Capacitor Preferences, and
  every key the app writes — the save blob included — lives in the single file
  CapacitorStorage.xml. `domain="sharedpref"` selects files, so per-key
  exclusion is not expressible here at all and no rewording of this file can
  make it so. Do not add the line back.

  The invariant it was reaching for now lives where both halves are visible at
  once: HomeWorkflowService.checkAndResumeQuiz refuses to resume a session
  whose state the hydrated save does not have spotted, whatever paired them.

  Nothing sensitive is stored — no account, no credentials, no location history
  (dec-0007-coarse-location-default). Location is read for one calculation and
  discarded.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
